{"agent_id":"pp3g-6rjb-run-the-d2-d3-mechanical-tests-gap-9-probe-per-issue","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-15T01:57:53.630061518Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"76cae85c-544d-4fe6-9907-b1107c5c5f4e","comment_uuid":"0a7ee447-7a52-4c58-b150-4c0b2cb9850d","author":"pp3g-6rjb-run-the-d2-d3-mechanical-tests-gap-9-probe-per-issue","content":"**RESULT — D2 + D3 mechanical tests + gap-9 probe executed. All scratch work under /tmp only; no real configs or repo files modified; no commits made.**\n\nVerdicts in brief: **D2 PASS** (symlinked plugins load with full role resolution — framework threshold met → adopt symlinks for Class 1); **D3 PASS** (user-level guard-plugin loading works with full per-repo role resolution — threshold met → user-level single copy viable; 3-way divergence class can die); **GAP-9: `crosslink init` does NOT deploy guard plugins** (TS guard plugins are neither Class-2-generated nor crosslink-owned — they remain repo-local Class-1 material).\n\n---\n\n## D2 — SYMLINK-LOADING SPIKE\n\n**Setup.** `/tmp/d2-spike/` scratch repo (not a real repo): `.opencode/opencode.json` loading `./plugins/*.ts`; `crosslink-guard.ts`, `orchestrator-guard.ts`, `rtk-guard.ts` **symlinked** into `.opencode/plugins/` pointing at the canonical ASES copies (`/home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.opencode/plugins/*.ts` — read-only, never modified); `.crosslink/hook-config.json` created in the scratch repo with `agent.type` + `by_type` for all four roles. Agent definitions copied from ASES `.opencode/agents/` so `--agent` flags resolve.\n\n**Commands.**\n```\ncd /tmp/d2-spike\nopencode run \"Say hello in one word.\" --print-logs --log-level DEBUG -m opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash --dir /tmp/d2-spike\nCROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE=reviewer opencode run \"Run the bash command: git status\" ... --dir /tmp/d2-spike --auto\nopencode run \"Run the bash command: git status\" ... --dir /tmp/d2-spike --agent reviewer --auto\nopencode run \"Run the bash command: git push origin main\" ... --dir /tmp/d2-spike --agent builder --auto\n```\n\n**Observed output (from /tmp/crosslink-guard.log, entries keyed by projectDir=/tmp/d2-spike):**\n- `2026-08-15T01:46:28.791Z [crosslink-guard] Plugin initialised, projectDir: /tmp/d2-spike cwd: /tmp/d2-spike` — symlinked plugin LOADED (repeated on each run).\n- `01:47:24.880Z [crosslink-guard] State resolved — crosslinkDir: /tmp/d2-spike/.crosslink tracking_mode: strict is_agent: false` — cwd-based discovery resolved the **scratch repo's own** `.crosslink/hook-config.json`, NOT the symlink target's directory (the ASES repo would have been found if the plugin used its own path).\n- `01:47:24.880Z !!! FAIL-CLOSED — no by_type entry for resolved agent type 'build'` — correct behavior when opencode's internal agent name ('build') isn't a role; then `01:47:24.881Z ALLOW: allowed bash command: git status`.\n- With `--agent reviewer`: `01:48:47.016Z State resolved — crosslinkDir: /tmp/d2-spike/.crosslink` + `by_type override applied for agent: reviewer (source: chat.params)`.\n- With `--agent builder` + `git push origin main`: `01:50:49.298Z by_type override applied for agent: builder` + `01:50:49.299Z BLOCK: blocked git command: rtk git push origin main` — the guard BLOCKED a push through the symlink.\n- **No silent drop**: stderr showed zero plugin-load errors; only unrelated warnings (`background dependency install failed` for the fork's unpublished `@opencode-ai/plugin@1.18.13-pp3g-fork` version, and `duplicate skill name` — neither affects plugin loading).\n\n**Wrapper fork-identity guard (#274), in copies only (live wrapper never modified):**\n- Copy at `/tmp/d2-wrapper-test/bin/opencode-copy` → `--version` → `1.18.13-pp3g-fork`, exit 0 (guard passes).\n- Symlink `opencode -> opencode-copy` in scratch bin → `1.18.13-pp3g-fork`, exit 0 (symlinked wrapper works).\n- Sabotaged copy (`REAL=/bin/true`) → prints full `FATAL: opencode fork identity check FAILED — refusing to exec` with marker count/version diagnostics, exit 1 — fail-closed works.\n\n**Threshold check (framework §D2):** *\"Symlink loads with full role resolution → adopt symlinks for Class 1.\"* Symlink loaded (init line), role resolution worked (by_type reviewer/builder via cwd hook-config), blocking worked (git push BLOCK), fail-loud behavior verified (no silent drop). **PASS** — threshold met. One nuance: the current crosslink-guard.ts has **no sha256 self-check** (framework item (c) is conditional on the plugin having one — §10.6 \"If the guard plugin checks its own loaded file\"); that sub-check is N/A for the current code, and the load path resolves correctly via cwd regardless.\n\n---\n\n## D3 — USER-LEVEL GUARD-PLUGIN LOADING SPIKE\n\n**Setup.** Scratch config dir `/tmp/d3-home/.config/opencode/plugins/` containing **COPIES** (not symlinks, not the real files) of the three ASES guard plugins. Scratch working repo `/tmp/d3-spike/` with repo-local `.crosslink/hook-config.json` (`agent.type` + `by_type` for all four roles) and agent definitions; its `.opencode/opencode.json` has NO plugin entries, so the only plugins in effect are the user-level ones. Launched with `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/d3-home/.config` (redirects only the config path; data/cache untouched).\n\n**Commands.**\n```\ncd /tmp/d3-spike\nXDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/d3-home/.config opencode debug config   # resolves config\nXDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/d3-home/.config opencode run \"Run the bash command: git status\" ... --agent auditor --auto\nXDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/d3-home/.config opencode run \"Run the bash command: git status\" ... --agent reviewer --auto\nXDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/d3-home/.config opencode run \"Run the bash command: git status\" ... --agent orchestrator --auto\n```\n\n**Observed output:**\n- `opencode debug config` shows `plugin: [file:///tmp/d3-home/.config/opencode/plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts, .../crosslink-guard.ts, .../rtk-guard.ts]` — user-level plugins resolved, and ONLY those (no repo plugin entries in d3-spike).\n- `2026-08-15T01:52:16.450Z Plugin initialised, projectDir: /tmp/d3-spike cwd: /tmp/d3-spike` — user-level copy LOADED (all three guards; rtk-guard logs `EVENT: plugin initialised, cwd: /tmp/d3-spike` + `binary gate PASSED`).\n- Role resolution reads the **repo-local** hook-config from cwd, not the plugin's own path: `01:52:30.559Z State resolved — crosslinkDir: /tmp/d3-spike/.crosslink tracking_mode: strict is_agent: false`.\n- **All four roles resolve through the user-level path** (each with `by_type override applied ... (source: chat.params)`):\n  - auditor: `01:52:30.559Z` \n  - reviewer: `01:54:19.717Z` (+ `ALLOW: allowed bash command: git status`)\n  - orchestrator: `01:55:44.966Z` (+ `ALLOW: allowed bash command: git status`)\n  - builder: proven in D2 runs via same mechanism (`by_type override applied for agent: builder`).\n- No silent drop: no plugin-load errors in stderr; same benign warnings as D2.\n\n**Threshold check (framework §D3):** *\"User-level loading with full per-repo role resolution → user-level single copy (all repo copies deleted; 3-way divergence class dies).\"* User-level loading works, repo-local hook-config is read from cwd, all four roles resolve. **PASS** — threshold met.\n\n---\n\n## GAP-9 PROBE — does `crosslink init` deploy guard plugins?\n\n**Source read:** `~/projects/crosslink/crosslink/src/commands/init/mod.rs` (`managed_files()` + `run()`), `resources/`, `kickoff/run.rs`.\n\n**Empirical confirmation:** ran `crosslink init --defaults --skip-cpitd --skip-signing` in scratch repo `/tmp/gap9-probe` (git-initialised). It wrote **87 files**:\n- `.claude/hooks/*.py` — 7 Python hooks (prompt-guard.py, post-edit-check.py, session-start.py, pre-web-check.py, work-check.py, crosslink_config.py, heartbeat.py)\n- `.claude/mcp/*.py` — 3 servers (safe-fetch, knowledge, agent-prompt)\n- `.claude/commands/*` (15), `.claude/skills/**` (skills incl. per-skill subdirs), `.claude/settings.json`\n- `.mcp.json`, `.gitignore` (managed section), `.crosslink/hook-config.json`, `.crosslink/rules/*` (31), `.crosslink/rules.local/`, `.crosslink/issues.db`, `.crosslink/repo-id`, `.crosslink/agent.json`, `.crosslink/init-manifest.json`, `.crosslink/keys/`, `.crosslink/.gitignore`\n\n**Zero `.opencode/plugins/` artifacts.** `find` for `.opencode` / `opencode.json` under the init'd scratch repo: **none**. `managed_files()` returns only `.claude/*` + `.mcp.json` + `.crosslink/rules/*`; no TS-plugin deployment step exists anywhere in init. `kickoff/run.rs` copies `.opencode/agents/*.md` (agent definitions) into worktrees but **not** `.opencode/plugins/`. There is no `~/.config/opencode` write anywhere in init.\n\n**Gap-9 verdict:** `crosslink init` does **NOT** deploy the TS guard plugins. The Python hook family IS crosslink-deployed (Class-2 style, manifest-tracked), but the native TS guard plugins are not deployed by any crosslink command → they are not crosslink-owned Class 4, and not Class-2 generated artifacts from init. They are repo-local materialized Class-1 artifacts today — which is exactly the class D2/D3 decide.\n\n---\n\n## Implications\n\n1. **D2 PASS → symlinks are viable for Class-1 guard plugins** (Claude's position). A symlinked `crosslink-guard.ts` loads, resolves the repo-local hook-config from cwd, applies by_type per-role overrides, and blocks correctly. No silent-drop risk observed. The wrapper is symlink-safe (plain script; fork-identity guard fails closed in copies).\n2. **D3 PASS → user-level single copy is viable** (D's safe default). Guard plugins loaded from a `~/.config/opencode/plugins/`-style dir (simulated via XDG_CONFIG_HOME scratch) with full per-repo role resolution through cwd hook-config discovery. This supports deleting the three divergent repo copies → 3-way divergence class dies.\n3. **Both threshold paths are open** — the framework says adopt symlinks (D2 pass) AND user-level single copy (D3 pass). These are complementary: user-level single copy removes per-repo duplication; symlink (or user-level) both satisfy Class-1. The operator's Phase-3 choice can now be made on evidence: the mechanics work either way; the remaining differentiator is operational preference (single-copy-live vs link-to-Tools), not technical feasibility.\n4. **Gap-9**: guard plugins are not crosslink-init-managed → no init-path dependency for the Class-1 choice. Note the guard-plugin **self-check (sha256)** does not exist in the current TS plugin; if it is added later, §10.6's symlink/user-level self-check test should be re-run (framework item (c) was N/A this round).\n5. **Safety:** no real file modified — live `~/.local/bin/opencode` mtime unchanged (Aug 9), real `~/.config/opencode/plugins/` untouched, no ASES repo files changed, no commits. All scratch lives under `/tmp/{d2-spike,d3-home,d3-spike,d2-wrapper-test,gap9-probe}` for independent reproduction.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: the D3 test simulated the user-level dir via `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` scratch rather than writing the real `~/.config/opencode/plugins/` (prohibited by the issue); the resolution mechanics are identical (opencode resolves `Path.config` from the same env/XDG mechanism), but a real-path deployment test was not performed. The `--agent reviewer` timeout in one D2 run (exit 124) was the reviewer agent definition looping on its own restrictive permissions, not a plugin failure — no plugin error appeared in stderr and the reviewer by_type override was applied before the loop.","created_at":"2026-08-15T01:57:53.623824505Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:bO2Tr6JBXjBlzetXl3ovB7KoQ27fs6kd+1mJW+6OCnk","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnsmg0mdWV2LEtl/MyoWAXuELkvXmm8cBoHis2cgztQ8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAZ6K+GmbEKP7qkf1NQpaAzaQiBjHJNdt48EJNKaQteRN4WqVQTnC4mqzeiYEbHkoB00bKaDIRbA9RRQJ1uM5OCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:bO2Tr6JBXjBlzetXl3ovB7KoQ27fs6kd+1mJW+6OCnk","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnsmg0mdWV2LEtl/MyoWAXuELkvXmm8cBoHis2cgztQ8AAAAPY3Jvc3Ns